lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p10-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p10 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[2]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text "10. The taskforce members confirmed that pre-ticked boxes to opt-in do not lead to valid consent as referred to either in the GDPR (see in particular recital 32 “Silence, pre-ticked boxes or inactivity should not therefore constitute consent.”) or in Article 5(3) of the ePrivacy Directive."@en .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p13
    a lgo:Provision ;
    eli:is_part_of lg:EDPB-CBT-2023 ;
    lgo:citation "Cookie Banner Taskforce report, para. 13" ;
    lgo:interprets lg:EU-2002-58-art5-3 ;
    lgo:regulates lgv:Consent ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[3]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p13-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p13 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[3]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text "13. The members agreed that for the consent to be valid, the user should be able to understand what they consent to and how to do so. In order for a valid consent to be freely given, the taskforce members agreed that in any case a website owner must not design cookie banners in a way that gives users the impression that they have to give a consent to access the website content, nor that clearly pushes the user to give consent (one way could be on the contrary to allow the continuation of the navigation without cookies from the first level in particular for example)."@en .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p14
    a lgo:Provision ;
    eli:is_part_of lg:EDPB-CBT-2023 ;
    lgo:citation "Cookie Banner Taskforce report, para. 14" ;
    lgo:interprets lg:EU-2002-58-art5-3 ;
    lgo:regulates lgv:Consent ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[3]/paragraph[2]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p14-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p14 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[3]/paragraph[2]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text """14. The taskforce members agreed that the following examples do not lead to valid consents (non-exhaustive list):
the only alternative action offered (other than granting consent) consists of a link behind wording such as ‘refuse’ or ‘continue without accepting’ embedded in a paragraph of text in the cookie banner, in the absence of sufficient visual support to draw an average user’s attention to this alternative action;
the only alternative action offered (other than granting consent) consists of a link behind wording such as ‘refuse’ or ‘continue without accepting’ placed outside the cookie banner where the buttons to accept cookies are presented, in the absence of sufficient visual support to draw the users’ attention to this alternative action outside the frame;"""@en .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p18
    a lgo:Provision ;
    eli:is_part_of lg:EDPB-CBT-2023 ;
    lgo:citation "Cookie Banner Taskforce report, para. 18" ;
    lgo:interprets lg:EU-2002-58-art5-3 ;
    lgo:regulates lgv:Consent ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[4]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p18-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p18 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[4]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text """18. Based on concrete examples, the taskforce members took the view that at least this practice could be manifestly misleading for users:
an alternative action is offered (other than granting consent) in the form of a button where the contrast between the text and the button background is so minimal that the text is unreadable to virtually any user."""@en .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p24
    a lgo:Provision ;
    eli:is_part_of lg:EDPB-CBT-2023 ;
    lgo:citation "Cookie Banner Taskforce report, para. 24" ;
    lgo:interprets lg:EU-2002-58-art5-3 , lg:EU-2016-679-art6-1 ;
    lgo:regulates lgv:Consent ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[5]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p24-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p24 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[5]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text "24. In this regard, the taskforce members took the view that non-compliance found concerning Art. 5 (3) in the ePrivacy directive (in particular when no valid consent is obtained where required), means that the subsequent processing cannot be compliant with the GDPR. Also, the TF members confirmed that the legal basis for the placement/reading of cookies pursuant to Article 5 (3) cannot be the legitimate interests of the controller."@en .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p32
    a lgo:Provision ;
    eli:is_part_of lg:EDPB-CBT-2023 ;
    lgo:citation "Cookie Banner Taskforce report, para. 32" ;
    lgo:interprets lg:EU-2002-58-art5-3 , lg:EU-2016-679-art7-3 ;
    lgo:regulates lgv:Consent ;
    lgo:requiresDisclosureOf lgv:ConsentWithdrawalMechanism ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[6]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p32-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p32 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[6]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text "32. Website owners should put in place easily accessible solutions allowing users to withdraw their consent at any time, such as an icon (small hovering and permanently visible icon) or a link placed on a visible and standardized place."@en .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p34
    a lgo:Provision ;
    eli:is_part_of lg:EDPB-CBT-2023 ;
    lgo:citation "Cookie Banner Taskforce report, para. 34" ;
    lgo:interprets lg:EU-2002-58-art5-3 , lg:EU-2016-679-art7-3 ;
    lgo:regulates lgv:Consent ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[6]/paragraph[2]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p34-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p34 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[6]/paragraph[2]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text "34. In addition to the requirements for the collection of consent to be valid in accordance with the GDPR and under Article 5(3) ePrivacy Directive, three additional cumulative conditions are mandatory (i) the possibility to withdraw consent, (ii) the ability to withdraw consent at any time, (iii) withdrawal of consent must be as easy as to give consent."@en .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p7
    a lgo:Provision ;
    eli:is_part_of lg:EDPB-CBT-2023 ;
    lgo:citation "Cookie Banner Taskforce report, para. 7" ;
    lgo:interprets lg:EU-2002-58-art5-3 ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[1]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p7-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p7 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[1]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text "7. As a preliminary remark, the task force members recalled that by default, no cookies which require consent can be set without a consent and that consent must be expressed by a positive action on the part of the user."@en .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p8
    a lgo:Provision ;
    eli:is_part_of lg:EDPB-CBT-2023 ;
    lgo:citation "Cookie Banner Taskforce report, para. 8" ;
    lgo:interprets lg:EU-2002-58-art5-3 ;
    lgo:regulates lgv:Consent ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[1]/paragraph[2]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI .

lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p8-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-p8 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-CBT-2023-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[1]/paragraph[2]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/other/report-work-undertaken-cookie-banner-taskforce_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text "8. When authorities were asked whether they would consider that a banner which does not provide for accept and refuse/reject/not consent options on any layer with a consent button is an infringement of the ePrivacy Directive, a vast majority of authorities considered that the absence of refuse/reject/not consent options on any layer with a consent button of the cookie consent banner is not in line with the requirements for a valid consent and thus constitutes an infringement. Few authorities considered that they cannot retain an infringement in this case as article 5(3) of the ePrivacy Directive does not explicitly mentioned a “reject option” to the deposit of cookies."@en .

